# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Netlify matches these rules TOP-DOWN and the FIRST match wins.
# The SPA catch-all at the bottom must stay last, or it will swallow
# everything above it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. Old Netlify subdomain -> custom domain.
#    Netlify does NOT do this automatically, even with a primary domain set.
#    The trailing "!" forces the redirect even though a file exists at the path.
http://aimeevandenbroekeportfolio.netlify.app/*   https://aimeevdb.com/:splat   301!
https://aimeevandenbroekeportfolio.netlify.app/*  https://aimeevdb.com/:splat   301!

# 2. Old case study slug -> new one (project renamed ADHD Quest -> Brownie Quest).
#    /adhd-quest was the only case study page Google had indexed, and it is
#    linked from an unpublished LinkedIn draft, so this must not 404.
/adhd-quest   /brownie-quest   301!

# 3. SPA fallback — MUST BE LAST.
/*    /index.html   200
